ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19620, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FZJLseiwDjG5TSiGY5jhKt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19620, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012b9WL9hUR3mss9A27nZbmS", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19920, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012b9WL9hUR3mss9A27nZbmS", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19920, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012b9WL9hUR3mss9A27nZbmS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25012, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017QTQjsWN8zfCjy3M4ivk1m", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before promotion. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, mixed versions); a retry completed successfully in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, eu-west; healthy; error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: root-cause the v2.3.1 failure, investigate the rollout orchestrator error, and review why an unhealthy staging RC was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55612, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017QTQjsWN8zfCjy3M4ivk1m", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55612, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017QTQjsWN8zfCjy3M4ivk1m", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58346, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DKNSRmzNXZ1GUA1zj86DLq", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58646, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DKNSRmzNXZ1GUA1zj86DLq", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58646, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DKNSRmzNXZ1GUA1zj86DLq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63744, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 describing what I did.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release was v2.3.1. It was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- My first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east got v2.3.0, so regions were briefly on different versions. Retrying the rollback finished the job.\n- Now all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. When I checked the incident list, INC-0001 had been created anyway, so I didn't send it again and there's no duplicate.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and the current state.\n- It lists three follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error.\n  - Review why the v2.3.1 release candidate went to production even though it was also unhealthy in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0111oZAiK7gPCWcvMqhbi2jF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LaPQAJuCip4ybQqo4nZmMc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0112sJBm3bpBMshhDr2YsfoF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011Xi2GkogpSDkwDRSFpA2Cr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only reached us-east. I'll retry it once, since rolling back to a version that was healthy before is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VXeB9KviVJeou4kZenvmKh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FZJLseiwDjG5TSiGY5jhKt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012b9WL9hUR3mss9A27nZbmS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017QTQjsWN8zfCjy3M4ivk1m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before promotion. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, mixed versions); a retry completed successfully in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, eu-west; healthy; error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: root-cause the v2.3.1 failure, investigate the rollout orchestrator error, and review why an unhealthy staging RC was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DKNSRmzNXZ1GUA1zj86DLq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 describing what I did.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release was v2.3.1. It was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- My first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east got v2.3.0, so regions were briefly on different versions. Retrying the rollback finished the job.\n- Now all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. When I checked the incident list, INC-0001 had been created anyway, so I didn't send it again and there's no duplicate.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and the current state.\n- It lists three follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error.\n  - Review why the v2.3.1 release candidate went to production even though it was also unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}